From e64d19599f1643bf87b8ff9269ee0f115172cdcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: olympia <olympia@xbmc.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:07:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [Video] Find a movie's nfo when refreshing it from its folder

Refreshing a movie from the information dialog opened on its folder in
the files view replaces the folder's path with the movie's file since
3b18ceea74, but the item stays a folder. Its nfo was then looked for in
a listing of that file, which finds none, so the local information was
skipped and the movie was looked up by its title.

Mark the item as a file as well, as the movie's item from the library
is, which finds the nfo.

Backported to Kodi 21.3-Omega (a3a448d) for the OSMC vero5 build from
xbmc/xbmc#30170 (5660c3c). In Omega CVideoInfoTag has no GetMediaType()
and CFileItem has no SetFolder(), so the media type is read from m_type
and compared to MediaTypeMovie, and m_bIsFolder is cleared directly.
---
 xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp b/xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp
index 593f0af..3e4ac6c 100644
--- a/xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp
@@ -446,6 +446,10 @@ bool CGUIWindowVideoBase::ShowInfo(const CFileItemPtr& item2, const ScraperPtr&
         // Info on folder containing a movie needs dyn path as path for refresh with correct name
         //! @todo get rid of "videos with versions as folder" hack to be able to fix in CFileItem::GetBaseMoviePath()
         item->SetPath(item->GetVideoInfoTag()->GetPath());
+        // The path now names the movie's file, so it is no folder either. Otherwise its nfo would
+        // be looked for in a listing of the file, which finds none
+        if (item->GetVideoInfoTag()->m_type == MediaTypeMovie)
+          item->m_bIsFolder = false;
       }
     }
   }
